  "color_morphology_note": "Colors in Numu follow a consistent morphological pattern. The base/adjective form ends in -kweta (e.g., Atsakweta = red). Adding -'a creates the predicate form meaning 'is [color]' (e.g., Atsakweta'a = is red). Adding -du creates the noun form meaning 'the [color] one' (e.g., Atsakwetadu = red one). The color root prefix can be compounded directly onto nouns (e.g., Atsa + Kwasu = Atsakwasu = red shirt). There are four distinct words for brown in the source material, possibly representing different shades or regional variants.",

