      "notes": "A complete Numu food prayer, presented in the source with the full Paiute text followed by a line-by-line translation. Poowa is the blowing blessing — a ritual sound/action performed at the beginning and end of the prayer. The prayer is reproduced exactly as laid out in the source material.",
